<script module>
  import Demo from "$ui/components/Demo.abide"
  import UploadDemo from "$ui/demos/rpc/uploads/UploadDemo.abide"
</script>

<main class="page">
  <h1>File uploads — multipart</h1>
  <p class="lead">A mutation whose single argument is a <code>FormData</code> accepts a file upload: the <code>File</code> rides in the multipart body, never in a JSON args object. The <code>files</code> schema validates the uploaded FILE (present, size, MIME); the JSON <code>input</code> schema validates the multipart TEXT fields (here <code>caption</code> is required and non-empty). Either failure is one 422 the client narrows to a <code>ValidationError</code>.</p>
  <Demo id="upload" title="<code>FormData</code> — multipart upload with file + text validation" server="src/server/rpc/rpcUpload.ts" client="src/ui/demos/rpc/uploads/UploadDemo.abide" tab="server">
    <UploadDemo />
  </Demo>
  <aside class="aside">
    <p>A native <code>&lt;form&gt;</code> builds the <code>FormData</code> for free: <code>new FormData(form)</code> harvests the <code>avatar</code> File and the <code>caption</code> text with no manual <code>.set()</code>. The browser then calls the SAME callable the server declares, which sends it as the raw multipart body — through the callable rather than the form's own <code>action</code>, because the CSRF gate wants a header a bare form submit can't forge.</p>
  </aside>
</main>
